{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>El who brought them out of Egypt.</b> Not on their own did they come forth, as you said, 'Behold, a people has come out of Egypt'; rather, it was He in His strength who brought them out, against the astrological decree that obligated them to remain there, and He showed on their behalf signs and wonders before the eyes of all. And just as He mentioned תרועה here, so He mentioned מוציאם here; and thus it says (II Samuel 7:23): ״אשר פדית לך ממצרים גוי ואלהיו״." "<b>Like the loftiness of the re'em for Him.</b> Like the strength of the re'em is His. And He likened His strength to the re'em, just as Scripture likened it to the lion, as it says (Hosea 11:10): ״ה׳ כאריה ישאג״ — for among the physical creations there is none greater than them in might, and the Torah spoke in human language in order to break it to the ear." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> כתועפות ראם לו — Balaam said: when He brings them down a little, He brings them down like a bird, as it says (Hosea 11:9 — ed.: ibid.): ״אפרים כעוף יתעופף כבודם״; and when He exalts them, He exalts them like a bird, as it says (Isaiah 60:8): ״מי אלה כעב תעופנה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {2 "The printed text cites שם ט (ibid. 9), i.e., Hosea 11:9, but the quoted verse אפרים כעוף יתעופף כבודם is Hosea 11:10 in the standard numbering; translated the citation as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:33.211500299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}